  "request": "Issue #1030: Amend a spec after work has started. The PR body must carry `Closes #1030`.\n\nOwner's settled decisions (do not re-ask):\n- A separate command, `speckit.companion.amend`, not a flag on specify. It edits the current spec.md in place.\n- It records each amendment in `.spec-context.json` as a new additive list field `amendments: [{at, by, what, why, replanned}]`, written by a new `write-context.py --amend '<json>'` flag (and accepted in `--batch`), appended without de-dupe. Not a new history kind: unknown kinds break the viewer schema, doctor and timing.\n- \"Big\" means a requirement was added or removed. Then amend reruns plan (`speckit.companion.plan`) and converge (`speckit.converge`, which appends tasks for the new requirements); a wording-only change reruns neither. Amend never moves the spec's status or step backward (the writer refuses that by design); on a completed spec it says so and points to Set status in VS Code to reopen it.\n- It ends with a keep-or-remove decision for code that no longer has a spec line (asked attended; unattended it records a concern instead).\n- The VS Code viewer's Overview shows one line in the intent block's context, after Replaces: \"Amended N times · last: <what>\". Update the viewer contract (types, zod schema), state derivation, the overview availability checks, the stories and tests, and add a changeset for speckit-viewer.\n- Register the command everywhere CI checks: extension.yml provides.commands, the tracked .specify/extensions/.registry, apps/speckit-extension/README.md command table and docs/commands.md, website reference/commands.mdx. Flat command body copying speckit.companion.resume.md (no nodes folder, so it stays out of the Workflow Builder). Leave the Copilot canvas out.\n- Changelogs: one `[Unreleased]` line in apps/speckit-extension/CHANGELOG.md (pipeline) and one in the root CHANGELOG.md for the Overview line (overview area). No version bumps.",
  "unattended": true,
